Build a Lexer and Parser for a mini command interpreter that supports three commands: SET var value (assigns a number to a variable), 
ADD var value (adds a value to an existing variable), 
and PRINT var (prints the variable's current value). All variable values are integers. If PRINT is called on an undefined variable, display an error message.

Required Tokens
SET
ADD
PRINT
ID
NUMBER
SET, ADD, PRINT: reserved keywords extracted from identifiers.

Grammar Rules
program : program cmd | cmd cmd : SET ID NUMBER | ADD ID NUMBER | PRINT ID

Sample Input
SET x 10 SET y 5 ADD x 3 PRINT x ADD y 20 PRINT y PRINT z

Expected Output
x = 13 y = 25 Error: variable 'z' is not defined

Hint: Keep a Python dictionary as your variable store.
In the p_cmd rule, use len(p) to distinguish between PRINT (3 tokens) and SET/ADD (4 tokens), or write separate functions.


